            "$v_2 = -\\frac{N_1}{N_2}v_1$",
            "$v_2 = \\frac{N_1}{N_2}v_1$"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The dotted ends always have the same polarity. The primary dot is at the top, so the top of $v_1$ is like the **bottom** of the secondary. Measured + at the top, $v_2$ has the opposite sign: $v_2 = -\\frac{N_2}{N_1}v_1$ (a 180° phase shift for AC)."
        },
        {
          "id": "q6",
          "type": "matchPairs",
